  Usenet has served as a venue for announcements and discussions on
  the \TeX\ ecosystem for over 40 years, and remains in operation
  despite the recent shuttering of the Web-to-news gateway on Google
  Groups.  This article (re)introduces readers to Usenet and its
  \code{comp.text.tex} newsgroup, discusses the implications of their
  severance from Google, and explains how users can continue to access
  them.
